  "verbalization": "Angoroside-C is consistently shown to have a target relationship with Caspase-5, which is further implicated in the targets Teyin and Pseudopterosin Q, all of which ultimately lead to SN12K1. This suggests a hierarchical pathway where Angoroside-C acts as a central node, directing its effects through Caspase-5, which in turn influences other molecular targets. The evidence supports a mechanism where Angoroside-C may modulate Caspase-5 activity, potentially triggering downstream signaling cascades that result in the activation of SN12K1. The presence of multiple targets in the chain indicates that Angoroside-C may exert its effects through a complex network of interactions, with Caspase-5 serving as a critical mediator. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Caspase-5 in linking Angoroside-C to SN12K1, suggesting a potential role in cellular processes that are regulated by this compound.",
